// CASE 7 — the actual cost of having no marker, isolated.
//
// CASE 6 already showed the stub does NOT suppress diagnostics: the checker
// carries on and reports defects in the finished functions too. So the cost
// is not blindness.
//
// This module is CORRECT apart from one unwritten function. Nothing here is
// wrong; `Weigh` is total and exhaustive and would run today. The question
// is whether a .beam comes out, because that is what decides whether you can
// RUN or TEST the finished half while the other half is unwritten.
module StubBlocks

type FrameType = :method | :header | :body | :heartbeat

// Complete, exhaustive, correct.
public int Weigh(FrameType f)

Weigh(:method) -> 1
Weigh(:header) -> 2
Weigh(:body) -> 3
Weigh(:heartbeat) -> 0

// Unwritten. The only thing in this module that is not finished.
public int Priority(FrameType f)
